From f5ee3cf16be3ea864a05a0fdba3113e51a314b7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 03:22:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 11/43] pvr: maxFramebufferLayers from the device, not a
 hardcoded 256 (-> 2048)

Same pattern as maxColorAttachments: pvr_arch_job_render.c asserts
layers <= PVR_MAX_FRAMEBUFFER_LAYERS, so the render path already accepts more than the 256
hardcoded in the limits struct. PVR_MAX_FRAMEBUFFER_LAYERS == PVR_MAX_ARRAY_LAYERS, which is
the same quantity the neighbouring maxImageArrayLayers already takes from
rogue_get_render_size_max_z(dev_info) - so use that, which also avoids pulling the csbgen
texstate header into this file (my first attempt used the macro directly and failed to build
on ROGUE_TEXSTATE_IMAGE_WORD1_DEPTH_MAX_SIZE).

maxFramebufferLayers now reads 2048, matching maxImageArrayLayers.

No regressions: bda, vk13, pctest, vk16, wgsize, samplers, storageimages, mrt all PASS;
glmark2 --validate still 0 failures / 27 pass; windowed 39 FPS unchanged.
---
 src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_physical_device.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_physical_device.c b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_physical_device.c
index 55e2a03..86617f5 100644
--- a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_physical_device.c
@@ -872,7 +872,11 @@ static bool pvr_physical_device_get_properties(
 
       .maxFramebufferWidth = max_render_size,
       .maxFramebufferHeight = max_render_size,
-      .maxFramebufferLayers = 256U,
+      /* Use the driver's own constant: pvr_arch_job_render.c asserts
+       * layers <= PVR_MAX_FRAMEBUFFER_LAYERS, so the render path already accepts more than
+       * the 256 hardcoded here. PVR_MAX_FRAMEBUFFER_LAYERS == PVR_MAX_ARRAY_LAYERS, which is
+       * the same device-derived maximum used for maxImageArrayLayers below. */
+      .maxFramebufferLayers = rogue_get_render_size_max_z(dev_info),
 
       /* Note: update nir_shader_compiler_options.max_samples when changing this.
        * 2x is included because the driver implements it: pvr_cr_isp_aa_mode_type()
